			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825728">
									

<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5949 is a VHS tape appearing to be a film with the title Survival Of Halloween. The sticker appears to be scratched off and written over with a black marker. Placing SCP-5949 into a VHS player will send the victim using SCP-5949 into the film through anomalous means. Any recordable devices and people in the room will be taken into SCP-5949, any means of contact will be disconnected, Only after everything gets transported may personnel enter into the room. Once inside the victim will now be trapped and can’t exit the SCP-5949. After 10 minutes being stuck, entities (we will now refer to as SCP-5949-1) will attempt to attack the victim stuck inside mainly by beating the victim to death and then eating the corpse. The film will only end when everyone dies.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -25 and three votes.</p>
<p>Rewrite by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quicksilvers" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3485737); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3485737&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606084134" alt="Quicksilvers" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3485737)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quicksilvers" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3485737); return false;">Quicksilvers</a></span> pending.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5127 is a collection of multiple scorpion glass flowers (also known as “forget-me-not’s”) inside a tawny brown clay pot filled with sandy loam soil.</p>
<p>During visual exposure to SCP-5127, all brain cells in the exposed subject relating to memory will soften and loosen up in a way that will discard any memories that would have been created during visual exposure. This effect will continue around 5 (five) minutes after exposure, but will cease after. Should the subject still be in effect from SCP-5127 despite the passing of 10 (ten) minutes or longer, they are to be put into recovery and will no longer be eligible for testing, unless directed otherwise by the 05 council. Nausea during a state of recovery is common.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -19 and three votes.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5458 is an anomalous Brunswick piano currently kept at Site-█. SCP-5458 must be constantly performed without any mistakes made when played. If any of this is violated, a transparent gas capable of corroding through human flesh will be released from the back of SCP-5458 within 20 seconds. The gas is classified as SCP-5458-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -15 and three votes.</p>
<hr />

